ChebyMap now supplies an iterative inverse by default for square maps with forward coefficients and no explicit inverse coefficients. The inverse uses analytic Chebyshev derivatives and confines its search to the forward domain. Unsolved positions are returned as AST__BAD. IterInverse can disable iteration or select it instead of an explicit inverse. NiterInverse defaults to four; TolInverse defaults to 1e-6 and measures corrections relative to each input domain's half-width.

This changes inverse availability for existing forward-only ChebyMaps, including objects read from older Channel dumps. Previously ignored explicit IterInverse settings now take effect. Explicit inverse coefficients remain preferred when IterInverse is unset. Ordinary PolyMap iteration retains its previous convergence and exhaustion rules.
